        "description": "2008-11-08. Captured into a 504 × 7,502 km polar orbit, lowered to 100 km on 2008-11-12. Released the Moon Impact Probe on 2008-11-14, which hard-landed at Shackleton crater near the south pole — making India the 5th national space agency to reach the lunar surface. Mission ended 2009-08-29 (10 months) when its power supply units failed. NASA's M³ data was later analysed to discover lunar surface water at >40 ppm."
